=========================================================
GOLDEN RULES
=========================================================

1. Use const whenever data should not change.

2. Pass large objects by const reference.

3. Mark getter functions as const.

4. Return const reference for read-only access to large members.

5. Use mutable only when logically the object's state doesn't change
   (cache, mutex, statistics).

6. Never use const_cast to modify an object originally declared const
   (Undefined Behavior).

7. Prefer const correctness throughout APIs—it makes code safer,
   clearer, and easier to maintain.
